# Build context exclusions.

# Never send local credentials into the Docker build context or bake them into
# an image. Keep only explicitly named example templates.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
#
# node_modules matters most: it exists on the developer's Windows machine with
# Windows-native binaries. Copying it into a Linux image would shadow the
# node_modules that `npm ci` installs in the builder stage and break the build
# in a confusing way. The image must always install its own.
**/node_modules

# frontend/build is now produced by the Dockerfile's builder stage rather than
# committed. Excluding it keeps a stale local build from entering the context.
frontend/build

# Not needed at runtime, and large.
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
.claude
docs
eva-ml-service
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
*.db
.venv
venv
env
**/.pytest_cache
**/coverage
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
